From: thunder
Subject: [PATCH] proc: require ptrace access to write /proc/<pid>/reclaim

CONFIG_PROCESS_RECLAIM (selected by the MediaTek ANDROID_DEFAULT_SETTING
bundle) creates /proc/<pid>/reclaim with mode 0222, and reclaim_write() walks
the target's VMAs and swaps out its anonymous pages without checking who is
writing. On Android only the SELinux policy limited the node to lmkd and
system_server; Thunder OS loads no policy, so any uid could evict the memory
of root daemons, PID 1 and other users' processes (security audit run 1:
uid 1000 moved 67 MiB of a root process to swap with one write).

Make the node owner-writable only and require PTRACE_MODE_ATTACH_FSCREDS on
the target, the rule upstream uses for process_madvise(MADV_PAGEOUT). The
in-kernel RTMM user calls the reclaim helpers directly and is not affected.
Thunder-specific; no upstream equivalent (the interface never went upstream).

--- a/fs/proc/base.c
+++ b/fs/proc/base.c
@@ -3018,7 +3018,7 @@
 	REG("mountinfo",  S_IRUGO, proc_mountinfo_operations),
 	REG("mountstats", S_IRUSR, proc_mountstats_operations),
 #ifdef CONFIG_PROCESS_RECLAIM
-	REG("reclaim", 0222, proc_reclaim_operations),
+	REG("reclaim", S_IWUSR, proc_reclaim_operations),
 #endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_PROC_PAGE_MONITOR
 	REG("clear_refs", S_IWUSR, proc_clear_refs_operations),
--- a/fs/proc/task_mmu.c
+++ b/fs/proc/task_mmu.c
@@ -1850,6 +1850,12 @@
 	if (!task)
 		return -ESRCH;
 
+	/* Mesma regra do process_madvise() upstream: quem escreve precisa poder ptrace o alvo. */
+	if (!ptrace_may_access(task, PTRACE_MODE_ATTACH_FSCREDS)) {
+		put_task_struct(task);
+		return -EACCES;
+	}
+
 	mm = get_task_mm(task);
 	if (mm) {
 		struct mm_walk reclaim_walk = {
